We have the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
4u - 5v &= 23 \quad \text{(1)} \\
2u + 4v &= -8 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}

To eliminate one of the variables, we can multiply equation (2) by 2 and then subtract it from equation (1) multiplied by 2. This will eliminate $u$ and allow us to solve for $v$.

Multiplying equation (2) by 2, we get:
\begin{align*}
2(2u + 4v) &= 2(-8) \\
4u + 8v &= -16 \quad \text{(3)}
\end{align*}

Now, we subtract equation (3) from equation (1):
\begin{align*}
(4u - 5v) - (4u + 8v) &= 23 - (-16) \\
4u - 5v - 4u - 8v &= 23 + 16 \\
-13v &= 39 \\
v &= \frac{39}{-13} \\
v &= -3
\end{align*}

Now that we have the value of $v$, we can substitute it back into one of the original equations to solve for $u$. Let's use equation (2):
\begin{align*}
2u + 4(-3) &= -8 \\
2u - 12 &= -8 \\
2u &= -8 + 12 \\
2u &= 4 \\
u &= \frac{4}{2} \\
u &= 2
\end{align*}

Now that we have the values of $u$ and $v$, we can find the value of $u+v$:
\begin{align*}
u + v &= 2 + (-3) \\
u + v &= -1
\end{align*}

Therefore, the value of $u+v$ is $\boxed{-1}$.
